From: erosqcfw <erosqcfw@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] update: keep the entries a cancelled walk did not reach

UpdateDirectory() unmarks every entry of a directory, walks it, then
purges whatever is still unmarked.  When the walk is cancelled (MPD
shutting down during an update), the loop stops early, so the purge
deletes every entry it had not reached yet, in this directory and in
every parent on the way back up.  UpdateService::Task() then sees
"modified" and saves that cut-down database.

On EROS Q every boot runs an update (S96sdscan), and mpd is stopped with
SIGTERM on power-off (mpd-persist), on every Extras game launch and on
entering USB file transfer mode.  Any of those during an update saved a
db that was missing the rest of the card (10-23: 3538 of 4277 songs);
the next boot then dropped the queue entries for the missing songs.

Skip the purge once cancelled.  The saved db keeps what the walk added
or updated plus everything it did not reach; the next complete update
still purges deleted files.

---
diff --git a/src/db/update/Walk.cxx b/src/db/update/Walk.cxx
index b322fbf..572df8d 100644
--- a/src/db/update/Walk.cxx
+++ b/src/db/update/Walk.cxx
@@ -375,6 +375,16 @@ UpdateWalk::UpdateDirectory(Directory &directory,
 		UpdateDirectoryChild(directory, child_exclude_list, name_utf8, info2);
 	}
 
+	if (cancel)
+		/* erosq: the loop stopped early, so every entry it did
+		   not reach is still unmarked; purging now would delete
+		   them from the database, and UpdateService saves the
+		   result.  A SIGTERM during an update (power-off, an
+		   Extras game, USB file transfer mode) used to cut the
+		   saved db down to the part already walked.  Keep the
+		   unvisited entries; the next update handles them. */
+		return true;
+
 	PurgeDeletedFromDirectory(directory);
 
 	directory.mtime = info.mtime;
